Part 4 — Note on Citation Inflation
During verification, the same real Cornell figure (11.2% price premium) was observed being progressively re-described across secondary sources with increasing confidence — from “one study by Cornell” to “the groundbreaking research” to a fabricated “2023 update, 30,000+ properties” with no locatable source. This is a general caution for VRYOH's own materials: cite the original Cornell/HBR sources listed above directly. Do not cite the secondary blogs that repeated them, even when those blogs appear frequently across search results.
